      <div style="font:500 12px var(--font-mono);color:var(--color-forest);letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:18px">/ Questions we get</div>
      <h2 style="font:600 var(--type-display-2)/1.08 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 40px;color:var(--color-forest);text-wrap:pretty">Questions we get</h2>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:28px 40px">
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">What if we do not have an OpenAPI spec?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Not a blocker. We reverse the surface from traffic, client code, and fuzzing. It adds a few days, and you get an inventory you did not have before.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Do you test GraphQL differently?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Yes. Introspection, query depth and complexity, batching abuse, and resolver-level authorization are all GraphQL-specific classes that REST testing does not cover.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">How many roles should we provide?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Every distinct permission level, including an unauthenticated baseline. Authorization bugs only appear when you compare what one role can reach against another.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Can you test internal APIs?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Yes, over VPN or a bastion host. Internal APIs often have weaker authorization because teams assume network isolation is enough.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
